**Stop collecting prompts. Install workflows. Run the ones that are implemented.**  
**别再收藏 Prompt 了：工作流可以安装，已经实现的可以直接跑。**

---

## What changed in v2 / v2 有什么不同

v1 proved that 100 useful workflows can be expressed honestly as Agent Skills. v2 fixes the next problem: **a good workflow definition is not the same thing as runnable software**.

因此 v2 把两个维度彻底拆开：

| Dimension | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Workflow status** | 这个工作流本身是否成熟、是否依赖外部集成、是否仍偏实验性 |
| **Implementation status** | 当前仓库有没有真正可以运行并经过 smoke test 的代码 |

Current registry:

- 🟢 **47 Verified Workflows** — workflow pattern is mature and auditable.
- 🔵 **33 Integration Required** — valid workflow, but needs API/App/OAuth/browser/database/infrastructure.
- 🟡 **20 Experimental / Assisted** — feasible, but quality or end-to-end reliability needs more review.
- ✅ **15 Tested Reference Implementations** — runnable from this repository and exercised by CI.
- 📘 **85 Definition-only Skills** — installable Agent Skills, but not falsely presented as executable runtimes.

See [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) for the v2 migration notes.

---

## Quick start

### A. Install a Skill definition into an Agent

```bash
npx skills add BryceYuuu/open-workflow-skills --list
npx skills add BryceYuuu/open-workflow-skills --skill video-bilingual-subtitles
```

`npx skills` is a **community ecosystem CLI**, not an OpenAI-official installer. Installing a Skill definition does not magically install FFmpeg, Pillow, OAuth credentials, browser sessions, or paid APIs.

### B. Run the local v2 runtime

```bash
git clone https://github.com/BryceYuuu/open-workflow-skills.git
cd open-workflow-skills

python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .

ows --version
ows list --implemented
ows doctor image-watermark
ows test
```

Optional local extras:

```bash
pip install -e '.[all]'
```

Run a skill:

```bash
ows run cron-builder -- --schedule "every monday at 9:30 am" --command "./backup.sh"

ows run data-cleaner -- \
  --input examples/customers.csv \
  --output output/customers-clean.csv \
  --dedupe email
```

The `--` separates `ows` arguments from the selected skill's own arguments.

