## Repository structure

```text
open-workflow-skills/
├── README.md
├── CHANGELOG.md
├── registry.json
├── pyproject.toml
├── open_workflow_skills/      # `ows` CLI
├── skills/                    # 100 Agent Skills
├── schemas/
├── scripts/
├── docs/
└── .github/workflows/validate.yml
```

---

## Evaluation / 测试

```bash
python3 scripts/validate_registry.py
ows test
```

CI checks:

- exactly 100 registered skills
- valid v2 workflow/implementation metadata
- required Agent Skill files
- required runtime files for the 15 implemented skills
- CLI smoke tests
- deterministic per-skill smoke tests

The rule remains simple: **do not ask an LLM to judge what code can verify mechanically.**

